* 18 Sep 26 dm - TEARDOWN (S.26).  ONE ADMINISTRATOR, SDSYS, AND IT IS AN OS
*   ACCOUNT, NOT A PERSON.  The old model - root drops to sdsys and
*   grant.administrator looks up the real person's register record and sdadmin
*   membership - is gone with it.  Two arms replace it:
*
*   ROOT IS REFUSED OUTRIGHT (W.5, the hard reading).  A root session is not
*   SD's administrator any more; the way in is a real login as sdsys.  Refusing,
*   instead of the old drop-and-ask, also stops SD from silently converting any
*   root invocation into an administrator session.
*
*   SDSYS, LOCAL ONLY (W.6).  A session that already runs as the sdsys OS user
*   is the administrator, PROVIDED it is a local session: SSH_CONNECTION and
*   SSH_TTY both empty.  ssh and the API tunnel both count as remote, and the
*   sdsys OS account is un-ssh-able at the sshd boundary as well; this test is
*   SD's own half of that door.  K$ADMINISTRATOR is set here and nowhere else
*   in GPL.BP - every other site reads it with -1.
*
* 18 Sep 26 dm, NIGHT - THE OWNER CORRECTED THE ROUTE, and the correction is
*   the rule: administration is by LOGGING IN as sdsys (its own password, at
*   the machine's keyboard or over a desktop-sharing view of it - VNC,
*   TeamViewer - which is a local login the OS itself provides), and there is
*   NO path from another user into sdsys.  "sudo -u sdsys sd" and "su - sdsys"
*   are refused (10195) exactly the way root is: both arrive as the sdsys OS
*   user on a local session, but the login that started them was somebody
*   else's, and the kernel's audit loginuid says so (K$LOGIN.UID - set once
*   by PAM at login, inherited by every descendant, unwritable without root).
*   The "sudo -u sdsys" route this block used to describe was the former
*   agent's suggestion and was never agreed to.  There is no plain sdsys
*   session either (owner): a login as sdsys IS the administrator, with every
*   admin verb - the Windows side's model exactly.
*
*   THE INSTALL BOOTSTRAP IS EXEMPT AND HAS TO BE (IS_INSTALL): while sd -i is
*   still building the machine there is no register and no finished CPROC, and
*   the seeding steps run as root.  That arm compiles only into the install
*   build of CPROC.
      if system(27) = 0 then           ;* entered as root?
$ifndef IS_INSTALL
         refuse.msg = sysmsg(10190)   ;* several lines: one DISPLAY each
         loop
            display remove(refuse.msg, refuse.more)
         while refuse.more
         repeat
* 07 Oct 26 dm - PAL-24, the owner's lower-case rule: the whole audit trail is lower case,
*   event names included ("all lower case", 7 Oct).  reason= is text and keeps its nouns.
         void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'elevation refused reason=root is not SD administrator')
         goto abort.cproc
$else
         void kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, 1)   ;* bootstrap: no register to read yet
$endif
      end
$ifndef IS_INSTALL
*   downcase: kernel(K$USERNAME, 0) is the OS account, and the comparison must
*   not depend on who typed what.
      if downcase(kernel(K$USERNAME, 0)) = 'sdsys' and env('SSH_CONNECTION') = '' and env('SSH_TTY') = '' then
         if kernel(K$LOGIN.UID, 'sdsys') = 1 then
            void kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, 1)
* 11 Sep 26 dm - PORT_ADOPTION 13.  Written AFTER the grant, the port's
*   PRE_RELEASE 98 ordering: a trail must not record rights not yet given.
            void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'elevation granted reason=sdsys login')  ;* 07 Oct 26 PAL-24: lower case
            admin.notice<-1> = sysmsg(10916)
         end else
* 18 Sep 26 dm, NIGHT - sdsys without a sdsys login: sudo, su, a service.
*   Refused like root; there is no plain sdsys session to fall back to.
            refuse.msg = sysmsg(10195)   ;* several lines: one DISPLAY each
            loop
               display remove(refuse.msg, refuse.more)
            while refuse.more
            repeat
            void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'elevation refused reason=sdsys session without a sdsys login')  ;* 07 Oct 26 PAL-24
            goto abort.cproc
         end
      end else
* 19 Sep 26 dm - SDSYS HAS NO REMOTE ACCESS AT ALL (owner, 19 Sep 2026: "sdsys
*   should not have any remote access from ssh or api").  REFUSED AT THE DOOR
*   NOW, not at the account.
*
*   WHAT IT WAS BEFORE, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED: the test above simply did
*   not match a remote sdsys session, so it got no grant and carried on; LOGIN
*   then refused it entry to the SDSYS account (login:334, 10002, audited).  So
*   the door was SHUT, and this is a hardening rather than a hole - but it was
*   shut one room further in, and a refusal at the door is what the owner's
*   ruling asks for and what root (10190) and a non-login sdsys (10195) already
*   get.  A session that should not exist should not start.
*
*   10191 WAS WRITTEN FOR EXACTLY THIS CASE IN THE TEARDOWN AND NEVER WIRED.
*   It was deleted earlier tonight as an orphan (S.34) and is restored here
